1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,207
Every time a workflow runs, Orchard Core creates an instance that records the run.

2
00:00:06,207 --> 00:00:10,645
In this video, you'll see how to list instances, follow what each one

3
00:00:10,645 --> 00:00:13,840
did, and retry or clean up the ones that failed.

4
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,307
A workflow is a definition:

5
00:00:20,307 --> 00:00:23,419
its activities, and the connections between them.

6
00:00:23,419 --> 00:00:27,833
Each time an event starts it, Orchard Core creates an instance, which is

7
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:32,020
one run of that definition, with its own values and its own history.

8
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:34,851
Some instances have not ended.

9
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:38,840
Halted means the instance waits for an event before it goes on.

10
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:41,557
Running counts the instances in progress:

11
00:00:41,557 --> 00:00:44,100
Idle, Starting, Resuming or Executing.

12
00:00:44,850 --> 00:00:46,541
The rest have stopped.

13
00:00:46,541 --> 00:00:50,166
Finished means the instance reached its last activity.

14
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:55,240
Faulted means an activity failed, and Aborted means the instance was canceled.

15
00:00:59,437 --> 00:01:01,214
Open Design, Workflows.

16
00:01:01,214 --> 00:01:06,483
A workflow that has instances shows an Instances badge, and the Instances button

17
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:10,097
in the toolbar lists the instances of every workflow.

18
00:01:10,571 --> 00:01:15,111
Each row shows the instance's ID, its status, the version of the workflow

19
00:01:15,111 --> 00:01:17,525
it runs on, and when it was created.

20
00:01:17,525 --> 00:01:21,951
The workflow's name comes first, and the newest instance is at the top.

21
00:01:22,445 --> 00:01:26,981
The counts above the list show how many instances have each status.

22
00:01:26,981 --> 00:01:29,466
Select Faulted to list only those.

23
00:01:29,466 --> 00:01:35,865
The drop-downs in the toolbar filter by workflow, status and creation date, and change the order.

24
00:01:40,096 --> 00:01:42,775
Select Halted, then open an instance.

25
00:01:42,775 --> 00:01:47,323
Its page shows the workflow ID, when it was created and its status,

26
00:01:47,323 --> 00:01:49,316
above the workflow itself.

27
00:01:49,774 --> 00:01:52,983
The workflow appears as it was when the instance started.

28
00:01:52,983 --> 00:01:57,262
The toolbar names the version the instance runs on, so changes published later

29
00:01:57,262 --> 00:01:58,434
do not affect it.

30
00:01:58,901 --> 00:02:03,896
The Blocking badge marks the activity the instance waits on, here Wait for payment.

31
00:02:03,896 --> 00:02:08,331
The activities and connections the instance ran are highlighted in green.

32
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:13,044
The Variables tab lists the variables of the workflow, with the values this

33
00:02:13,044 --> 00:02:16,240
instance has, such as the order number it started with.

34
00:02:16,695 --> 00:02:20,879
The Journal tab lists the activities the instance ran, in order.

35
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:24,705
Select one to open its panel, then select its Details tab.

36
00:02:24,705 --> 00:02:30,205
Under This instance, it says Waiting on this activity or Not waiting on this activity.

37
00:02:34,422 --> 00:02:37,906
Back on the list, select Faulted and open an instance.

38
00:02:37,906 --> 00:02:42,377
A faulted instance adds a Fault Message to the details, which shows the

39
00:02:42,377 --> 00:02:44,002
error that stopped it.

40
00:02:44,457 --> 00:02:49,567
On the canvas, a red outline marks the activity that faulted, here Check stock.

41
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:54,197
Nothing after it is highlighted, because the instance never reached it.

42
00:02:54,652 --> 00:02:59,204
In the Journal tab, each record shows the activity, its status and how

43
00:02:59,204 --> 00:03:02,319
long it took, and its outcome when it has one.

44
00:03:02,319 --> 00:03:06,272
The record of the failed activity carries the error instead.

45
00:03:06,737 --> 00:03:08,415
Select the failed record.

46
00:03:08,415 --> 00:03:12,422
The activity panel opens on its Runs tab, which lists every time the

47
00:03:12,422 --> 00:03:15,617
instance ran that activity, and the error of the run.

48
00:03:16,083 --> 00:03:21,017
After you fix the cause, such as a service that was down, select Retry from here.

49
00:03:21,017 --> 00:03:26,461
A dialog explains that the instance runs again from this activity, with its current state.

50
00:03:26,461 --> 00:03:29,523
Retrying needs the Execute workflows permission.

51
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:34,860
Confirming runs the instance again, and a message reports the status it reached.

52
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:37,975
A retry uses the version the instance started on.

53
00:03:37,975 --> 00:03:43,410
To use a later version, select Restart, which starts another instance with the same input.

54
00:03:47,619 --> 00:03:52,549
To act on several instances at once, check two or more in the list.

55
00:03:52,549 --> 00:03:56,669
An Actions menu appears, with Retry, Cancel and Delete.

56
00:03:57,145 --> 00:04:02,117
Retry runs the faulted instances again from the activity they faulted at, and

57
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:03,913
leaves the others alone.

58
00:04:03,913 --> 00:04:08,405
A message says how many ran again, and how many could not be retried.

59
00:04:08,868 --> 00:04:14,427
Cancel sets every checked instance that is not Finished to Aborted, faulted ones included.

60
00:04:14,427 --> 00:04:17,496
Halted instances stop waiting for their events.

61
00:04:17,496 --> 00:04:20,218
Delete removes the instances you checked.

62
00:04:22,218 --> 00:04:24,279
An instance records one run:

63
00:04:24,279 --> 00:04:28,583
its status, the activities it ran, and the error that stopped it.

64
00:04:28,583 --> 00:04:32,402
From the list, you can retry, cancel or delete instances.

65
00:04:32,402 --> 00:04:33,978
Thanks for watching.

